Save this supplied index.html beside main.js:
```html
<div id="topics"><button type="button" data-topic="read"><span id="icon">Read</span></button><p id="blank">No action</p></div>
```
querySelector finds the named element. addEventListener registers onClick for click events; removeEventListener later removes that same callback. MouseEvent(type, options) constructs a synthetic event and dispatchEvent sends it synchronously through DOM listeners. This tests propagation, not a trusted human click.
```javascript
function installDelegation(root, log) {
  function onClick(event) {
    const button = event.target.closest("button[data-topic]");
    if (!button || !root.contains(button)) return;
    log.push({topic: button.dataset.topic,
      target: event.target.id, current: event.currentTarget.id});
  }
  root.addEventListener("click", onClick);
  return () => root.removeEventListener("click", onClick);
}
const root = document.querySelector("#topics");
const log = [];
const dispose = installDelegation(root, log);
const icon = document.querySelector("#icon");
icon.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent("click", {bubbles: true}));
console.log(JSON.stringify(log));
dispose();
```
Output: [{"topic":"read","target":"icon","current":"topics"}].

after:
This page puts a span inside a button. Save it as `index.html` beside `main.js`.
```html
<div id="topics"><button type="button" data-topic="read"><span id="icon">Read</span></button><p id="blank">No action</p></div>
```
Here is the JavaScript for that page.
```javascript
function installDelegation(root, log) {
  function onClick(event) {
    const button = event.target.closest("button[data-topic]");
    if (!button || !root.contains(button)) return;
    log.push({topic: button.dataset.topic,
      target: event.target.id, current: event.currentTarget.id});
  }
  root.addEventListener("click", onClick);
  return () => root.removeEventListener("click", onClick);
}
const root = document.querySelector("#topics");
const log = [];
const dispose = installDelegation(root, log);
const icon = document.querySelector("#icon");
icon.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent("click", {bubbles: true}));
console.log(JSON.stringify(log));
dispose();
```
Output:
```text
[{"topic":"read","target":"icon","current":"topics"}]
```
The click starts on `icon`, but the listener runs on `topics`. The guard line returns early if no suitable button was found.

`MouseEvent` creates a test click. `bubbles: true` lets it travel up to the group. `dispatchEvent` sends it through the listeners right away.
